\title{cosmet: Analysis of Ecotoxicological Mesocosm Experiments}
\description{
Analyses the data of aquatic mesocosm and microcosm experiments with chemicals, from the validation of the design to the effects on populations and communities. Compares every treatment with the control for each taxon and sampling date with the step-down test of Williams (1972) \doi{10.2307/2556164} or the test of Dunnett (1955) \doi{10.1080/01621459.1955.10501294}, derives no observed effect concentrations with optional criteria for consistent effects, computes minimum detectable differences following Brock et al. (2015) \doi{10.1007/s11356-014-3398-2}, and fits and tests principal response curves (van den Brink and ter Braak 1999 \doi{10.1002/etc.5620180207}) with 'vegan'. Includes the counts of the azoxystrobin mesocosm experiment of Amador et al. (2024) \doi{10.1016/j.aquatox.2023.106828}.
}
